    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/who-we-are": {
      "title": "Who we are",
      "description": "Who we are - Jobs @ Charles Sturt Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Who we are Who we are Charles Sturt University is defined by a national vision built on regional opportunity, collaboration, a sense of community, flexibility, a focus on individuals and results. We believe that building opportunity in the communities we serve also builds opportunity for all Australians. Next Prev 1 2 3 4 Our mission For the Public Good We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. Acknowledging the culture and insight of Indigenous Australians, Charles Sturt's ethos is described by this phrase from the Wiradjuri, the traditional custodians of the land of our original campuses: 'yindyamarra winhanga-nha' ('the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in'). Our values Our values guide the way we work and the way we approach each other, including students, colleagues and our communities. Derived from our ethos, our values are to be insightful, inclusive, impactful and inspiring. By living these values, we want to make this a world worth living in. Our Sustainability Commitment Proud to be Australia’s first certified carbon neutral university , we have a strong track record in achieving sustainability outcomes. Drawing on national and international connections and partnerships we are building on our success. Our recently released Sustainability Statement looks to the future, affirming our commitment to sustainable practice both within and beyond the University. Knowledge and innovation Knowledge and innovation are a central part of our business. Working in close partnership with industry, our research centres in agriculture, theology, ethics and environmental science develop new knowledge, identify solutions to problems and support industry innovation. Fast Facts Campus locations: We have campuses located in Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Canberra, Dubbo, Goulburn, Orange, Parramatta, Port Macquarie and Wagga Wagga. We also have study centres located in Melbourne and Sydney, as well as in several regional locations. Student base: We deliver tertiary education both on campus and online to approximately 38,000 students located across Australia and internationally. Graduate employment rate: 83.6 per cent of Charles Sturt graduates are in full-time employment within four months of graduation Employee recognition Letting our staff know they are doing a great job is important. It may be a 'thank you', a letter of appreciation or encouragement to take on a new challenge. We recognise the contribution of our employees to our success and celebrate the high achievement of our staff through an annual awards program. Through employee development and review discussions, staff have the opportunity to seek feedback on their individual performance, as well as set goals and objectives for the year ahead. Academic excellence We invest in innovation and excellence in learning and teaching. Focusing on key areas significant to Charles Sturt's mission, we support the development of research expertise. We continually improve our learning and teaching through a strong evaluation framework and support for the development of academic capability. Indigenous recognition Charles Sturt's regional campuses are located within the nations of the Wiradjuri, Gundungarra, Ngunnawal and Biripi people. Charles Sturt University acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands on which its campuses are located, paying respect to the Elders, both past and present, and extending that respect to all Indigenous Australians. Staff in the spotlight Dr Shokoofeh Shamsi - Senior Lecturer in Veterinary Parasitology \"I joined Charles Sturt University in January 2010 from Melbourne where I was doing a postdoc at RMIT. I started at Charles Sturt as a lecturer in parasitology in the School of Animal and Veterinary Sciences a job that I had dreamed of for a long time. I could teach and do research at the same time both of which are among my main passions in life. After living in capital cities and working in major universities my entire life I was ... a bit uncertain at first about my decision to come to Wagga and join a regional university. After almost 7 years I now know I made one of the best decisions ever. Charles Sturt is relatively a new university in Australia and particularly due to being located in a regional area the opportunities for innovative research, taking leadership roles and make impact in science and the community is immense. Life in Wagga Wagga is very peaceful. No time or energy is wasted in traffic for example. For those with families, it is much easier to manage responsibilities such as taking kids to extra-curricular activities for which plenty of opportunities are available, along with a busy academic life. Most Charles Sturt campuses are located just few hours drive from the capital cities, making weekend escapes easy and joyful.\" Show more chevron_right Shaarn Hayward - Indigenous Student Success Coordinator \"I have been working for Charles Sturt University in various roles on the Port Macquarie campus now for 3 years. Two of the best things about working at Charles Sturt is the people and the rewarding feeling my job gives me. The staff are extremely helpful. By having staff across all campuses there is a huge range of experience and a wealth of knowledge. I love my job and what I do. I enjoying working in a role that I know makes a p ... ositive difference on so many people's lives. Being a part of Charles Sturt Port Macquarie has been so exciting. I often have people in the community asking me about the campus and saying how great it is to have Charles Sturt in Port. There is a sense of community spirit that is associated with this campus and its great being a part of it. People no longer have to leave the area to get a quality tertiary education. It has also brought jobs into Port Macquarie and without Charles Sturt I wouldn't be able to have a job that I love in the place that I love. Show more chevron_right Designs Folder expand_more Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries expand_more Phone: 1800 275 278 International: +61 1800 275 278 Enquire Here 'Yindyamarra Winhanganha' - The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and\n            present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri,\n            Ngunawal, Gundungurra, and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land\n            where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Jobs @ Charles Sturt Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries Contact us Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram Youtube LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Registration and Regulatory Status | Disclaimer & Copyright | Accessibility | Privacy"
    },
    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/benefits": {
      "title": "Benefits",
      "description": "Benefits - Jobs @ Charles Sturt Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Regional living Financial benefits Health benefits Professional development Childcare Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Benefits Benefits As part of working with us at Charles Sturt University, you will enjoy a number of benefits including a great work-life balance, professional development opportunities and generous financial benefits. Work-life balance We offer a range of generous leave options, providing our staff with the flexibility they need to balance work and personal commitments. This includes 20 days annual leave, 15 days personal leave, generous parental leave and more. Regional Living When you join Charles Sturt at one of our regional campuses, you will share in the benefits of regional living, including reduced commute times and affordable housing. Find out more chevron_right Financial benefits There are a number of financial benefits at Charles Sturt beyond your normal salary, including employer superannuation between 12% and 17% and a range of discounted goods and services through our corporate partner program. Eligible employees are also able to access a range of salary packaging options. Find out more chevron_right Health benefits We encourage our staff to live a healthy lifestyle, offering free professional counselling services, a range of sporting facilities at many of our campuses and discounts at a range of gyms. Staff also have the opportunity to participate in a variety of scheduled health and wellbeing events and activities. Find out more chevron_right Professional development We offer a range of professional development opportunities. At Charles Sturt professional development is more than formal training. Staff have the opportunity to learn through on the job experience, stretch objectives and coaching. Find out more chevron_right Childcare Our campuses at Albury-Wodonga, Wagga Wagga and Bathurst have on-site childcare centres open to both the public and Charles Sturt employees. As these centres cater to the needs of the community as well as Charles Sturt Staff members, we encourage to you to contact the centres early to secure your child a place. Find out more chevron_right Designs Folder expand_more Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries expand_more Phone: 1800 275 278 International: +61 1800 275 278 Enquire Here 'Yindyamarra Winhanganha' - The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and\n            present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri,\n            Ngunawal, Gundungurra, and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land\n            where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Jobs @ Charles Sturt Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries Contact us Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram Youtube LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Registration and Regulatory Status | Disclaimer & Copyright | Accessibility | Privacy"
    },
    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/applying": {
      "title": "Applying",
      "description": "Applying - Jobs @ Charles Sturt Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying Before you apply How to apply Preparing for your interview International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Applying Applying As part of applying for one of our positions at Charles Sturt University, is it important that you understand our application process and requirements. Application requirements can differ depending on the type of job you’re interested in. Before you apply Before you start your application, you should ensure you have a good understanding of the role and of Charles Sturt University in general. Before you apply chevron_right How to apply Depending on whether you’re applying for an academic, professional or general position, the information you’ll need to include in your application will vary. How to apply chevron_right Preparing for your interview At Charles Sturt, our interview processes are designed for you to show us your interest in the position and the skills, experience and values you bring to the university. Prepare for your interview chevron_right Designs Folder expand_more Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries expand_more Phone: 1800 275 278 International: +61 1800 275 278 Enquire Here 'Yindyamarra Winhanganha' - The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and\n            present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri,\n            Ngunawal, Gundungurra, and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land\n            where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Jobs @ Charles Sturt Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries Contact us Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram Youtube LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Registration and Regulatory Status | Disclaimer & Copyright | Accessibility | Privacy"
    },
    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/international-applicants": {
      "title": "International applicants",
      "description": "International applicants - Jobs @ Charles Sturt Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Relocating to Australia Living in Australia Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt International applicants International applicants Moving to Australia to take up a position with Charles Sturt University can be a challenging prospect. In this section, we provide you with important information about relocating and living in Australia. Relocating to Australia As part of moving to Australia, you will need to consider: The type of visa you and your dependants require The financial implications of relocating The process of relocating family, possessions and pets Whether you need temporary accommodation Find out more chevron_right Living in Australia There are a number of aspects of living in Australia that you need to be aware of, including: How our finance and banking systems work Getting health care to suit your needs Organising education for your children (if required) Transport arrangements, especially in regional areas Your long term accommodation plans Australian Culture Find out more chevron_right Designs Folder expand_more Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries expand_more Phone: 1800 275 278 International: +61 1800 275 278 Enquire Here 'Yindyamarra Winhanganha' - The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and\n            present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri,\n            Ngunawal, Gundungurra, and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land\n            where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Jobs @ Charles Sturt Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries Contact us Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram Youtube LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Registration and Regulatory Status | Disclaimer & Copyright | Accessibility | Privacy"
    },
    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/contact-us": {
      "title": "Contact us",
