    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/vacancies": {
      "title": "Vacancies",
      "description": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - {page-title listing=\"Recent Jobs\" search=\"Search Results\" detail=\"Details - [job.title]\"} {css} \n {javascript} Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Vacancies Vacancies Charles Sturt University uses the PageUp recruitment system to manage job applications and candidate information. This means certain personal information applicants provide when applying for a job with CSU will be hosted on PageUp’s systems. See the PageUp FAQs for further information provided to job seekers . If you haven't applied for a job with us before, view our tips on how to apply to get you started. You can also find out more about Charles Sturt University before you apply. Existing Applicant? LOGIN Job Alerts? {job-mail-subscribe-link} Sign up {/job-mail-subscribe-link} {form}\n{messages no-job-message=\"Sorry, we can't provide additional information about this job right now.\"}\n{search-filters button-text=\"Filter Results\"} by Keyword {search-keyword placeholder=\"Search CSU jobs\"} Clear All {pages}\n{/form}"
    },
    "https://www.pageuppeople.com/faqs/": {
      "title": "Frequently asked questions",
      "description": "We value your privacy We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, serve personalised ads or content, and analyse our traffic. By clicking \"Accept All\", you consent to our use of cookies. Read more Reject All Accept All Powered by Customise Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorised as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site. ... Show more For more information on how Google's third-party cookies operate and handle your data, see: Google Privacy Policy Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyse the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customised advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyse the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. Other Other uncategorised cookies are those that are being analysed and have not been classified into a category as yet. Reject All Save My Preferences Accept All Powered by LLMs.txt Frequently Asked Questions - PageUp the template is tpl-faq-page.php < Back Skip to content Products Products Talent Acquisition Suite Your complete hiring platform Discover more Recruitment Marketing & CRM Attract, engage and nurture great talent Applicant Tracking System Create exceptional hiring experiences Onboarding Deliver a seamless start for new employees PageUp AI Purposeful intelligence for modern TA Paige Agentic AI Agentic hiring assistant that shows its work. Employee Connections Text Engage Analytics Learning Performance Succession Marketplace Work your way with seamless integrations Solutions Solutions By industry Government Healthcare Higher Education Mining and Construction Retail By size Enterprise Mid-market By use case DEI Internal Mobility Resources Resources The Talent Marketing Playbook Success story : Texas Christian University Explore how to attract, engage, and convert top talent with less effort. Blog Read about the future of work, innovation and HR technology. Events & webinars Join us live and interactive at a range of digital events. Ebooks, guides and more Dive into PageUp’s in-depth resources for HR teams and business leaders. Product tours Explore PageUp products in action with our quick, interactive tours. Customer stories See how teams around the world use PageUp to delight employees. ROI calculators Calculate how much you could save with PageUp software. Talent quest quiz See how well your team is navigating today’s talent landscape. Recruitment metrics industry benchmark tool See how your organisation measures up against critical industry data. About About About us Contact us Security PageUp newsroom Careers Sign in Sign in Client Training Book a meeting Sign in Sign in Client Training Book a meeting Subscribe Get started Frequently asked questions Choose the category that best suits you and browse our answers to common questions Job seeker Information for someone who is in the process of applying for a role that has been posted by a PageUp client organisation organization Job seeker Client employee Suitable for an employee of a PageUp client organisation organization – typically a hiring manager, or an employee accessing their performance and/or talent review Client employee System user FAQs for an employee of a PageUp client organisation organization ’s HR function, who has backend access to that organisation organization ’s PageUp powered talent management software System user Job seeker Information for someone who is in the process of applying for a role that has been posted by a PageUp client organisation organization Who Is PageUp? PageUp builds software people love to use. Our HR software is used by organisations organizations globally, to improve their talent management practices. As a result, our technology powers many job application and careers sites. For more information on your job application process and technical questions related to it, please check out some of the common scenarios below and our relevant recommendations. How do I apply for a job? You can search and apply for jobs on the career site of the organisation organization that you wish to apply to. When you apply for a job, you will be asked to complete personal details and an application form as determined by the organisation organization to which you are applying. PageUp is a human resource software-as-a-service provider, and not an employment provider or executive search agency. As such, we are not involved in your application process other than supplying the organisation organization that you are applying to with the software platform on which it is run. How do I access my application? If you have previously applied to the organisation organization , you already will have a profile with them (identified by your email address) and will be asked for your password. I have forgotten my password. What do I do now? When asked for your password, you will also be presented with a link ‘Don’t know your password?’. If you have forgotten it you can click this and reset instructions will be emailed to you. If you do not receive the email within 2 minutes, please check your spam/junk folder. If the email is not received, it may be that your email service provider has lost the email. In this case, it’s recommended that you commence a new application with a different email address. The email account that’s registered to my profile is no longer valid. How do I get access to my profile now? Please contact the organisation organization to which you are applying for a job, directly. For security reasons PageUp is unable to make any amendments to your profile or provide you with information directly. Who do I contact about my application or recruitment process? Please contact the organisation organization to which you are applying for any questions related to the recruitment process and/or outcomes. Being a service provider, PageUp is unable to provide any information in this regard. How do I delete my personal details or get access to information held in my profile? Please contact the organisation organization to which you are applying to request this. Such information is owned and governed by the organisation organization and its associated privacy statement, and not by PageUp. For security purposes, PageUp is unable to fulfil requests directly from applicants. Where can I find PageUp’s privacy policy? All information is owned and governed by the organisation organization and its associated privacy statement, and not by PageUp. You can view the organisation organization ’s privacy statement when you apply for a job via the relevant link. If you have any questions please contact the organisation organization directly. Why does PageUp have access to my Google Drive? PageUp offers applicants the option to upload documents for their application which are hosted on Google Drive. You may be prompted with a dialog to allow the system to access the documents in your account. Click the “Accept” button to ensure that you can upload documents into your application. Once permission has been granted, it will remain in place so that should you wish to upload documents from your google drive for any future applications with PageUp clients it will be available. Please see Google’s internal documentation should you wish to rescind access. NOTE : PageUp will not use any uploaded google documents into its Application other than for the intended purpose, as described when uploading the documentation. Why am I receiving job alert emails from @mail.pageuppeople.com? PageUp will occasionally send emails to job seekers who’ve registered to receive job alert emails via an organisation organization ’s PageUp-hosted career site. To update your subscription, please contact the relevant organisation organization . To unsubscribe, please use the link in the footer within the last received email. Client employee Suitable for an employee of a PageUp client organisation organization – typically a hiring manager, or an employee accessing their performance and/or talent review How do I log in? Please go to our login page via the PageUp homepage. How do I reset my password? If you are a system user and do not know your password, please click on ‘Don’t know your password’ to initiate the reset process. Please note that you will need your security keyword. If you do not know your security keyword, please contact your internal HR Team. How do I access training and onboarding material for the PageUp System? To access your system training and onboarding, login and select ‘Knowledge Portal’ from the information button. If you don’t have this option in the list, please contact your internal Super User or System Administrator. How do I raise a support case? To access support, please select ‘Raise support case’ from the information button once you are in the system. If you don’t have this option in the list, please contact your internal Super User or System Administrator. If you are having issues accessing your PageUp account, please contact your internal Super User/System Administrator. If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team. Who are the Super Users/System Administrators of my PageUp System? Super Users or System Administrators are designated individuals in your HR team that have been granted full administrative and access rights to the PageUp platform you are using. If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team who will be able to direct you to them. What if I Have Other Queries That Are Not Covered Above? All other support requests and technical questions that are not covered above should be directed to the Super User/System Administrator at your organisation organization . If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team who will be able to direct you to them. Your Super User/System Administrator will be able to raise a case with the PageUp Support team. System user FAQs for an employee of a PageUp client organisation organization ’s HR function, who has backend access to that organisation organization ’s PageUp powered talent management software How do I log in? Please go to our login page via the PageUp homepage. How do I reset my password? If you are a system user and do not know your password, please click on ‘Don’t know your password’ to initiate the reset process. Please note that you will need your security keyword. If you do not know your security keyword, please contact your internal HR Team. How do I access training and onboarding material for the PageUp System? To access your system training and onboarding, login and select ‘Knowledge Portal’ from the information button. If you don’t have this option in the list, please contact your internal Super User or System Administrator. How do I raise a support case? To access support, please select ‘Raise support case’ from the information button once you are in the system. If you don’t have this option in the list, please contact your internal Super User or System Administrator. If you are having issues accessing your PageUp account, please contact your internal Super User/System Administrator. If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team. Who are the Super Users/System Administrators of my PageUp System? Super Users or System Administrators are designated individuals in your HR team that have been granted full administrative and access rights to the PageUp platform you are using. If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team who will be able to direct you to them. What if I Have Other Queries That Are Not Covered Above? All other support requests and technical questions that are not covered above should be directed to the Super User/System Administrator at your organisation organization . If you do not know who your Super User/System Administrator is, please contact your internal HR team who will be able to direct you to them. Your Super User/System Administrator will be able to raise a case with the PageUp Support team. Products Recruitment Marketing Employee Connections Text Engage Applicant Tracking System Onboarding Analytics Learning Performance Succession Marketplace Solutions Purposeful AI Mid-market Enterprise Healthcare Retail Higher Education Government Mining and Construction Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Internal Mobility Collaborative Hiring Company About us Careers PageUp Newsroom FAQs Resources Product Tours ROI Calculators Recruitment Metrics Industry Benchmark Tool Talent Quest Quiz Glossary From our blog Here’s what the best career sites have in common The shift to proactive hiring Building a continuous recruitment pipeline Read more blogs... Contact us eArcu privacy policy PageUp privacy policy Modern slavery statement Responsible Disclosure Security The Talent Marketing Playbook Build a hiring engine that attracts, engages and converts the right candidates even when your team isn’t online. Get your copy"
    },
    "https://www.csu.edu.au/jobs/information-for-applicants": {
      "title": "Information for applicants",
      "description": "Information for applicants - Jobs @ Charles Sturt Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Information for applicants Information for applicants Message from the Vice-Chancellor and President Charles Sturt University is a relatively young university but one with strong roots in in our communities and with a proud history of education and research which serve regional Australia. We are a multi-campus institution across a large geographic footprint in regional Australia, as well as campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Canberra. At the heart of our work is the Wiradjuri phrase Yindyamarra Winhanganha : ‘the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in’. Our staff are passionate and energetic in serving this ethos and our mission to build skills and knowledge in our regions. Our staff enjoy a collegial environment, meaningful work, and the opportunity to contribute to resilient, sustainable communities. At Charles Sturt University, we believe in making a difference. I hope you will consider doing the same through the fulfilling and exciting roles we have to offer. Learn more about Charles Sturt University Our University We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. Learn more chevron_right Our Strategy Our University Strategy 2020 - 2030 set an ambitious and transformative agenda for the University. Learn more chevron_right What we do With more than 30 years of experience leading and innovating online education in Australia, Charles Sturt offers the most comprehensive range of programs of any university. Learn more chevron_right Our history Whilst we've been a university for more than 20 years, our history of professional education and research spans more than 100 years. Learn more chevron_right Our locations Our NSW campuses are in some of Australia's fastest growing regional cities. We offer a unique study experience with access to the best of city living and the benefits of a regional lifestyle. Learn more chevron_right Benefits As part of working with us, you'll enjoy a number of benefits including a great work-life balance, professional development opportunities and generous financial benefits. Learn more chevron_right Designs Folder expand_more Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries expand_more Phone: 1800 275 278 International: +61 1800 275 278 Enquire Here 'Yindyamarra Winhanganha' - The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and\n            present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri,\n            Ngunawal, Gundungurra, and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land\n            where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Jobs @ Charles Sturt Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Enquiries Contact us Stay Connected Facebook Twitter Instagram Youtube LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Registration and Regulatory Status | Disclaimer & Copyright | Accessibility | Privacy"
    },
