    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/499098/senior-information-analyst": {
      "title": "Vacancies",
      "description": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - Details - Senior Information Analyst Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Vacancies Vacancies Charles Sturt University uses the PageUp recruitment system to manage job applications and candidate information. This means certain personal information applicants provide when applying for a job with CSU will be hosted on PageUp’s systems. See the PageUp FAQs for further information provided to job seekers . If you haven't applied for a job with us before, view our tips on how to apply to get you started. You can also find out more about Charles Sturt University before you apply. Existing Applicant? LOGIN Job Alerts? Sign up Work type All Work types Continuing - Full Time (1) Locations All Locations Albury-Wodonga (1) Bathurst (1) Dubbo (1) Orange (1) Wagga Wagga (1) Categories All Categories Information Technology (1) by Keyword Clear All Senior Information Analyst Apply now Reference no: 499098 Work type: Continuing - Full Time Location: Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Wagga Wagga Categories: Information Technology Attractive salary and benefits including 17% super Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support a healthy work-life balance Thrive in a dynamic, purpose-driven, and collaborative team The role Full Time, Continuing Level 8 - $113,948 to $128,980 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange or Wagga Wagga. Remote work considered upon application. As the Senior Information Analyst, you will partner with senior leaders across the University to understand complex organisational challenges, identify the underlying business issues, and translate diverse data into clear, actionable insights. Operating as a trusted analytical advisor, you will develop robust reports, dashboards and analytical products that inform strategy, governance, planning and evidence-based decision-making. About you A trusted analytical partner who can engage stakeholders, challenge assumptions and shape evidence-based solutions Skilled in investigating complex information needs and translating analysis into clear strategic advice Strong communication and influencing skills, with the ability to brief senior decision-makers with clarity Advanced capability in Excel, SQL, Tableau/Power BI, data cubes and related analytical tools Experience in higher education, institutional performance, quality evaluation or compliance is highly regarded About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Office of Planning and Analytics here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Katie Dunn | Manager, Performance and Reporting | kadunn@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 9 September 2026 Advertised: 26 Aug 2026 09:00 AM - AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 09 Sep 2026 11:00 PM - AUS Eastern Standard Time Apply now Refer a friend Back to search results Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results - showing: 0 Position Location Closes Senior Information Analyst Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Wagga Wagga 9 Sep 2026 11:00 PM Use evidence-based analysis to solve complex challenges and shape University strategy. Current Vacancies Position Location Closes Senior Information Analyst Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Wagga Wagga 9 Sep 2026 Use evidence-based analysis to solve complex challenges and shape University strategy. Expression of interest Casual Employment Register Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. Powered by PageUp"
