    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/498968/lecturer-in-midwifery": {
      "title": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - Details - Lecturer in  Midwifery",
      "description": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - Details - Lecturer in  Midwifery Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Vacancies Vacancies Charles Sturt University uses the PageUp recruitment system to manage job applications and candidate information. This means certain personal information applicants provide when applying for a job with CSU will be hosted on PageUp’s systems. See the PageUp FAQs for further information provided to job seekers . If you haven't applied for a job with us before, view our tips on how to apply to get you started. You can also find out more about Charles Sturt University before you apply. Existing Applicant? LOGIN Job Alerts? Sign up Work type All Work types Continuing - Full Time (1) Locations All Locations Orange (1) Categories All Categories Academic - Teaching Focussed (1) by Keyword Clear All Lecturer in  Midwifery Apply now Reference no: 498968 Work type: Continuing - Full Time Location: Orange Categories: Academic - Teaching Focussed Flexible teaching model with regional impact Supportive academic team and career development Join an innovative and student-centred learning environment The role Full Time, Continuing Level B - $113,841 to $134,965 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Orange We are seeking an experienced and motivated academic to join our School of Nursing, Paramedicine and Healthcare Sciences as a Lecturer in Midwifery. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to a highly respected postgraduate midwifery program while helping shape the next generation of healthcare professionals. You will deliver engaging and contemporary learning experiences across a range of teaching modes, including face-to-face, online and intensive delivery. You will contribute to curriculum development, student success, scholarly activity and, where relevant, research aligned with the University's strategic priorities About you Registration as a Registered Midwife with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (AHPRA) A doctoral or master's qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent professional experience Demonstrated clinical currency and contemporary midwifery expertise Experience delivering student-centred education in higher education or professional settings Strong communication, collaboration and stakeholder engagement skills Commitment to culturally safe practice and inclusive education About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Faculty of Science and Health here . Learn more about the School of Nursing, Paramedicine and Healthcare Sciences here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of di