    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/498822/agripark-casual-employment-register": {
      "title": "Vacancies",
      "description": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - Details - AgriPark Casual Employment Register Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Vacancies Vacancies Charles Sturt University uses the PageUp recruitment system to manage job applications and candidate information. This means certain personal information applicants provide when applying for a job with CSU will be hosted on PageUp’s systems. See the PageUp FAQs for further information provided to job seekers . If you haven't applied for a job with us before, view our tips on how to apply to get you started. You can also find out more about Charles Sturt University before you apply. Existing Applicant? LOGIN Job Alerts? Sign up Work type All Work types Casual (1) Locations All Locations Wagga Wagga (1) Categories All Categories Sustainability (1) by Keyword Clear All AgriPark Casual Employment Register Apply now Reference no: 498822 Work type: Casual Location: Wagga Wagga Categories: Sustainability What is the AgriPark Casual Employment Register? The AgriPark Casual Employment Register allows individuals to express interest in casual agricultural and farm‑based work at the University. When short‑term or seasonal work opportunities arise within AgriPark, the University reviews this register and may contact suitably skilled candidates to discuss potential casual engagements. Being on the register does not guarantee employment; however, it enables us to quickly connect with people who have relevant skills and availability when needs arise. Who should apply? We welcome expression of interest from individuals with relevant skills and experience in one or more of the following areas; General farm labour Livestock handling and animal care Biosecurity Soil sampling Cropping operations Horticulture and/ or vineyard work How Does It Work? 1. Express Your Interest Complete the online application form and provide details about your: Skills and experience Availability Preferred location (if applicable) Pay rate expectations 2. Stay on the Register Your application will remain active on the register for up to six (6) months. You may update or withdraw your application at any time if your circumstances change. 3. Potential Opportunities If a casual or temporary opportunity becomes available that matches your skills and availability, you may be contacted to discuss the role. 4. Employment Conditions Casual employees are engaged by the university in accordance with applicable industrial and statutory requirements. How to Apply If you are interested in joining the AgriPark Casual Employment Register , please apply online and complete the application form. For further information, please contact jobs@csu.edu.au Advertised: 01 Apr 2026 09:00 AM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 11:00 PM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Apply now Refer a friend Back to search results Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results - showing: 0 Position Location Closes AgriPark Casual Employment Register Wagga Wagga 31 Oct 2026 11:00 PM Are you looking for casual opportunities in agriculture or farm-based work? Current Vacancies Position Location Closes AgriPark Casual Employment Register Wagga Wagga 31 Oct 2026 Are you looking for casual opportunities in agriculture or farm-based work? Expression of interest Casual Employment Register Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. Powered by PageUp"
    },
    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/498107/casual-employment-register": {
      "title": "Vacancies",
      "description": "Vacancies - Jobs @ Charles Sturt - Details - Casual Employment Register Skip to main content Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt search Home Vacancies Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Jobs @ Charles Sturt Welcome Vacancies redirect Who we are Benefits Applying International applicants Contact us Future Students Staff Alumni Library Faculties & Schools Jobs News About Contacts Student Portal Jobs @ Charles Sturt Vacancies Vacancies Charles Sturt University uses the PageUp recruitment system to manage job applications and candidate information. This means certain personal information applicants provide when applying for a job with CSU will be hosted on PageUp’s systems. See the PageUp FAQs for further information provided to job seekers . If you haven't applied for a job with us before, view our tips on how to apply to get you started. You can also find out more about Charles Sturt University before you apply. Existing Applicant? LOGIN Job Alerts? Sign up Work type All Work types Casual (1) Locations All Locations Albury-Wodonga (1) Bathurst (1) Dubbo (1) Orange (1) Port Macquarie (1) Wagga Wagga (1) Categories All Categories Administration (1) Building and Property Services (1) Catering Services (1) Child Care (1) Customer Service (1) Data Analysis (1) Dentistry (1) Finance (1) Health Services (1) Human Resources (1) Information Technology (1) Library (1) Marketing (1) Professional (1) Research (1) Research Assistant (1) Student Services (1) Technical Officer (1) by Keyword Clear All Casual Employment Register Apply now Reference no: 498107 Work type: Casual Location: Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Port Macquarie, Wagga Wagga Categories: Finance, Administration, Human Resources, Information Technology, Library, Marketing, Research, Building and Property Services, Research Assistant, Technical Officer, Catering Services, Child Care, Student Services, Data Analysis, Customer Service, Health Services, Dentistry, Professional Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. What is the Casual Employment Register? Our Casual Employment Register is for people interested in working at the university on a casual basis in non-academic roles. When temporary needs arise, we review the register and contact suitable candidates to discuss potential assignments. Please note if you are looking for casual academic work visit our casual academic register . Who Should Apply? We welcome expressions of interest from individuals with relevant skills and experience in areas such as: Administration Child Care Customer service Facilities and Maintenance Finance Hospitality Information Technology Learning and Teaching Support Library Marketing & Communications Research Radio Technical and specialist higher education support roles How Does It Work? Express Your Interest – Complete the online application form, including information about your skills, experience, availability, preferred location, and pay rate expectations. Stay on the Register – Your details will remain on our register for up to three months. If your circumstances change, you can update or remove your information. Potential Opportunities – When a casual/temporary role becomes available that matches your skills and availability, we may contact you to discuss the opportunity. Employment Conditions – Casual employees are engaged by the university in accordance with applicable industrial and statutory requirements. Benefits of joining Flexibility – Pick up work that suits your schedule. Experience – Gain valuable experience in different roles and departments. Potential for continuing roles – While there are no guarantees, casual roles can sometimes lead to longer-term employment opportunities for those who are interested in permanent roles. How to Apply If you’re interested in joining our Casual Employment Register , please apply now and complete an application. For further information, contact jobs@csu.edu.au . We look forward to hearing from you! Advertised: 27 Mar 2025 09:00 AM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Dec 2026 11:00 PM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Apply now Refer a friend Back to search results Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results - showing: 0 Position Location Closes Casual Employment Register Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Port Macquarie, Wagga Wagga 31 Dec 2026 11:00 PM Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. Current Vacancies Position Location Closes Casual Employment Register Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Port Macquarie, Wagga Wagga 31 Dec 2026 Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. Expression of interest Casual Employment Register Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. Powered by PageUp"
    }
